### The coach: a second pair of eyes

After each paper fill, and when you submit an order, the rule-based coach reviews the trade and writes short notes into your journal entry. It looks for the habits that sink new traders:

- risk above roughly 1–2% of equity, or **no stop at all**;
- a reward-to-risk below 1.5;
- trading against the 50-day trend;
- a [[Revenge trading|revenge trade]] opened within minutes (or two bars) of a loss;
- [[Overtrading|overtrading]], more than five trades in a day;
- one position above 25% of equity;
- adding to a losing position (averaging down).

Each note is a *tip* or a *warning* and links to the lesson that explains it. The coach does not know whether the trade will work, and it never tells you to buy or sell. It checks your process against your own rules. Treat a warning as a question to answer in your journal, not an insult: *"Why did I skip the stop this time?"*
